    <!-- ============================================================ -->
    <!-- Using the notes with Obsidian on a computer -->

    <string name="obsidian_title">Using with Obsidian</string>
    <string name="obsidian_intro">An Obsidian vault is a folder of Markdown files, which is what Notes keeps. What is needed is a way to get the same files onto the computer.</string>
    <!-- Shown only while the notes are in a folder on the phone. %1$s is a place, e.g. "Documents/Notes on this phone\'s storage" -->
    <string name="obsidian_copy_heading">Copying by hand</string>
    <string name="obsidian_copy">The notes are plain .md files in %1$s. Plug the phone into a computer by USB and copy that folder across, then open it as a vault: no sync and nothing else to install.</string>
    <string name="obsidian_copy_place">%1$s on this phone\'s storage</string>
    <string name="obsidian_copy_unknown">the folder you chose</string>
    <string name="obsidian_webdav_heading">A WebDAV service</string>
    <string name="obsidian_webdav">Keep the notes on a WebDAV service such as Koofr, which is free up to 10 GB and gives app passwords for WebDAV. Its desktop app keeps a folder on the computer the same as the one on the service, and that folder opens as a vault.</string>
    <string name="obsidian_davx5_heading">A DAVx5 mount</string>
    <string name="obsidian_davx5">If you already use DAVx5, its WebDAV mounts put a WebDAV folder in the phone\'s folder picker, and Notes can keep its notes there as a folder on this phone. The mount reads from the server as files are opened, so there is no copy to open without a signal and no merging of two people\'s edits; a WebDAV server chosen in Notes itself keeps a copy here and merges.</string>
    <string name="obsidian_syncthing_heading">Syncthing</string>
    <string name="obsidian_syncthing">Install Syncthing-Fork on the phone and Syncthing on the computer, and sync a folder on the phone with one on the computer, with no server between them. Keep the notes in the phone\'s folder and open the computer\'s as a vault; both have to be on for changes to cross. Obsidian rewrites .obsidian/workspace.json all the time, so add the ignore pattern .obsidian/workspace* in Syncthing on both, or it makes conflict copies.</string>
    <string name="obsidian_nextcloud_heading">Nextcloud</string>
    <string name="obsidian_nextcloud">Keep the notes on your Nextcloud, and let the Nextcloud desktop app keep the folder on the computer. Open that folder as a vault.</string>
    <string name="obsidian_sync_heading">Obsidian Sync</string>
    <string name="obsidian_sync">Obsidian\'s own paid sync, through Obsidian on the phone. Open the synced vault there once, move it in Manage vaults to a folder such as Documents, and keep the notes in that folder.</string>

